# Drumming and dancing in inala, Brisbane on a hot Monday

Today we ventured off in the hot sun to Inala, Brisbane in the DJ Sherrington Park - The Hut. We gathered a group under a big tree and shared some African rhythms with Wesley Mission Queensland. Everyone was feeling the heat but still we had lots of drumming solos, smiles and laughs. During the workshop, we had members of the community come  and join us just because they could hear us from where they were in the neighbourhood. The Wesley Mission Group welcomed them with a chair and a drum. Such a lovely, open and inclusive bunch of people. Our highlight was a lovely man who enjoyed the workshop so much, he participated for the entire dance and then wrote down the words for the African song. We all sang, we all drummed, we all danced in Inala, Brisbane under a big tree on a hot Monday. Life is Good!
